{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 37,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "At this also my heart trembleth, and is moved out of its place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear attentively the noise of his voice, and the sound ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " goeth out of his mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He directeth it under the whole heaven, and his lightning to the ends of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "After it a voice roareth: he thundereth with the voice of his excellence; and he will not stay them when his voice is heard.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God thundereth marvelously with his voice; great things he doeth, which we cannot comprehend.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he saith to the snow, Be thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "on",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the earth; likewise to the small rain, and to the great rain of his strength.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He sealeth up the hand of every man; that all men may know his work.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the beasts go into dens, and remain in their places.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "From the south cometh the whirlwind: and cold from the north.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By the breath of God frost is given: and the breadth of the waters is straitened.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also by watering he wearieth the thick cloud: he scattereth his bright cloud:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it is turned around by his counsels: that they may do whatever he commandeth them upon the face of the world on the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He causeth it to come, whether for correction, or for his land, or for mercy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hearken to this, O Job: stand still, and consider the wondrous works of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Dost thou know when God disposed them, and caused the light of his cloud to shine?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Dost thou know the balancings of the clouds, the wondrous works of him who is perfect in knowledge?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How thy garments ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " warm, when he quieteth the earth by the south ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "wind",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hast thou with him spread out the sky ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " strong, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as a molten looking-glass?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Teach us what we shall say to him; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " we cannot order ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "our speech",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by reason of darkness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall it be told him that I speak? If a man shall speak, surely he will be swallowed up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And now ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " see not the bright light which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the clouds: but the wind passeth, and cleanseth them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fair weather cometh from the north: with God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " terrible majesty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Touching",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the Almighty, we cannot find him out: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " excellent in power, and in judgment, and in abundance of justice: he will not afflict.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.37.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.37.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Men therefore fear him: he respecteth not any ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wise of heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
